Slight lie. It can depend on exactly one covariate.

f(name,cov,copy=copy_name, hyper=list(beta=list(fixed=FALSE)))

Where cov is the covariate.  This is an example of the poorly documented "weight" option, which annoyingly doesn't pop up in autocomplete. If I remember correctly, there's an example of spavilly varying covariate weights, which uses the same mechanism, in the slides on either dat 2 or 3 of this http://www.math.ntnu.no/~daniesi/INLA/StAndrews/

D

